From 585659d56f6593c1b99164ac1dc8243bb92d9882 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:37:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 086/101] MAS local: draw the lean window's title bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The lean window on Windows used the system title bar for minimize and
close, and kept back and home in a column right of the guest screen. Now
the window draws its own title bar: the window icon and title on the
left, then back, home, a divider, minimize and close, with Chinese tool
tips (返回, 桌面, 最小化, 关机). The column is gone; the guest screen sits
right under the title bar. The palette is the column's, on Windows 10 and
11 alike. ANDROID_EMU_FULL_TOOLBAR=1 and headless instances are as
before.

To Qt the window is frameless. Windows gets the caption style back, with
WM_NCCALCSIZE making the whole window client area: that keeps the DWM
shadow and border, and with DWMWCP_ROUND the rounded corners of Windows
11. There is no resizable frame and no maximize box, and the window is
moved by the title bar and resized by its edges here, in
WindowsLeanFrame, never in the system's move and size loops. So Windows
does not snap, dock or maximize it: no Aero Snap at the screen edges, no
maximize on a double click or Win+Up, and no Windows 11 layout flyout.
Maximize and the keyboard move and size are refused as system commands,
and the system menu (Alt+Space, right click on the title bar) keeps only
minimize and close. Close, from the title bar, the system menu, Alt+F4 or
the taskbar, is the safe shutdown as before.

A drag keeps the grabbed point of the title bar under the cursor when the
window moves onto a screen with another scale. A resize keeps the guest
screen's aspect ratio and fits the guest screen once released. The
resize bands lie inside the window: 5 px along the left, right and
bottom edges, 4 px along the top, 16 px at the corners (logical pixels).

The window's size around the guest screen is now ToolWindow::windowChrome(),
the title bar's height, where the code added the column's 54 px width.
The guest screen no longer starts at the window's top-left corner, so the
GPU subwindow, a child of the whole window, is placed with the offset of
the guest screen's area (skin_winsys_get_content_offset(); zero headless
and without the title bar), and so is the zoom overlay.
The window title (ModAVD#58, the instance name) is worked out by
instance_window_title(), the arithmetic of the frame by lean-window-frame,
both without a windowing system and tested in
aemu-ui-lean-window_unittests.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#58
Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#59

